"""
council.py — Round 0 / Round 1 debate engine for the MAGI council (ADK build).

The agent-call layer was migrated off Letta Cloud onto the Google Agent
Development Kit (ADK). Each council member is a native ADK `LlmAgent` with a
locked `output_schema` (structured JSON) and `include_contents="none"` (stateless
per cycle); council.py runs them and TRANSLATES their structured output back into
the exact parsed-vote dict shapes orchestrator.py already consumes, so the
boundary is unchanged.

Boundary preserved — orchestrator.py imports and calls, unchanged:
  update_world_state(world_state)
  run_round_0_parallel(cycle_id, world_state=None) -> {agent: vote_dict}
  should_run_r1(round_0, prior_signature=None)     -> (fire: bool, reason: str)
  run_round_1(round_0, cycle_id)                   -> {agent: r1_vote_or_error}
  resolve_consensus(round_0, round_1, conflict=None) -> consensus dict
  emit_human_alert(cycle_id, reason)

Parsed-vote dict shape returned for each agent (UNCHANGED from the Letta build —
this is the contract resolve_consensus / enforce_hard_rules / _build_debate_record
read):
  casper:    {position(regime), conviction(float), key_evidence[list], crux,
              regime_action, freshness_retry, _raw}
  melchior:  {position(grid_action), conviction(float), key_evidence[list], crux,
              geometry({target_spacing_pct,target_levels} | None),
              freshness_retry, _raw}
  balthasar: {position(risk_action), conviction(float), key_evidence[list], crux,
              geometry_veto, freshness_retry, _raw}

`_raw` carries the un-translated native vote (RegimeVote/GridVote/RiskVote dump)
so Round 1 can paste peers' votes in their NATIVE vocabulary. Downstream consumers
read only the documented keys; `_raw` is ignored by them.

VERDICT -> grid_action mapping (Melchior). The new GridVote emits an economic
verdict, not the old action vocabulary; orchestrator/engine still consume
grid_action ∈ {MAINTAIN, RECENTRE, TIGHTEN, WIDEN}. council.py maps:
  THESIS_HOLDS       -> MAINTAIN   (no geometry)
  RECONFIGURE        -> RECENTRE   (geometry = chosen variant; engine rebuilds to it)
  NO_PROFITABLE_GRID -> MAINTAIN   (no geometry)
This is lossy by design (TIGHTEN/WIDEN are not emitted; NO_PROFITABLE_GRID does
not actively tear down a live grid — it holds). See the migration report.

Action vocabularies after translation (unchanged downstream contract):
  - casper.position    ("regime")      : RANGING | TRENDING | UNCERTAIN
  - melchior.position  ("grid_action") : MAINTAIN | RECENTRE | TIGHTEN | WIDEN
  - balthasar.position ("risk_action") : CLEAR | PAUSE_LONGS | PAUSE_SHORTS | HALT

NOTE: model invocation requires google-adk + litellm installed and the provider
keys in the environment (GOOGLE_API_KEY for Gemini, OPENAI_API_KEY for GPT-4o,
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for Claude). ADK is imported lazily so importing this module
(and therefore orchestrator.py) does not hard-require it.
"""

